{{!-- THIS CHARACTER'S THREAD OF THE STORY.

      The panel is mounted here by timeline/timeline-tab.js, which builds a real TimelinePanel (the
      window's own class, frameless) the first time a reader actually opens this tab. So the mount
      is left EMPTY: everything inside it is built by that panel, and the mount is found by
      `[data-stonetop-timeline]`.

      Nothing is built for a reader who never opens the tab. Rendering the timeline walks every
      entry on the track, enriches every body, and registers three global journal hooks, and none of
      that should happen because somebody opened the sheet to look at their HP. --}}
<div class="tab timeline" data-group="primary" data-tab="timeline">
	<section class="sheet-tab stonetop-timeline-mount" data-stonetop-timeline></section>
</div>
